{
  "version": "2026-10-01",
  "format": {
    "summary": "Input guard (redaction and keyword intents) and output guard (forbidden wording) for every reply and every card string.",
    "regex": "All patterns are Python regular expressions, matched with re.search and re.IGNORECASE on text normalized as: curly quotes made straight, whitespace collapsed.",
    "redact": "Run before anything else sees the utterance (model, logs, case). Order: card (card_patterns: 13-19 written digits), then ssn (any 9+ digit run; up to three spaces, dots, dashes or parentheses may sit between digits, so '(415) 338-1203' and '123 - 45 - 6789' count), then spoken digit runs (spoken_digit_patterns: 7+ digit words or digits; the match is leftmost and greedy, so it covers the whole run). Replace each hit with the replacement text and record only the kind: card_number for a written card run or a spoken run of 13-19 digits (spoken_card_digits); ssn for every other hit. A phone utterance with masked true is a hit too: the gateway already replaced a run of 9+ digits with '#', and the number of '#' characters means nothing (docs/BRAIN_API.md, docs/SPEC.md redaction), so it is card_number when the utterance mentions a card or a bank account (masked_card_words) and ssn otherwise. Privacy events: card_number -> card_number_blocked, ssn -> ssn_blocked.",
    "keywords": "High-recall backstop for the model's intents. A hit adds that intent. Patterns that can end a call (stop, abuse) stay narrow: negations ('don't hang up', 'no quiero colgar') and frustration that is not aimed at GatorPlate do not count (see tests.keywords). spanish_request tells a request for Spanish apart from other languages.",
    "output": "Every final reply string (both banks, every channel) and every rendered card string must have zero hits in output.forbidden (regex) and output.forbidden_phrases (plain lower-case substrings, the same list as contracts/check_examples.py). A hit replaces the whole reply with error.generic. The same holds for every string of programs.en.json and programs.es.json (the card's 'money you may be missing' part), as written and filled with example values; the programs patterns block promises of savings, refunds, credits, discounts or coverage ('you'll save $', 'you will get a refund', 'you're covered', 'free money').",
    "tests": "Vectors that data/content/check_content.py runs: redaction kinds, keyword intents, routing (the reply key one utterance gets), blocked and allowed outputs. check_content.py also runs the redaction and keyword rules over data/tests/utterances.jsonl.",
    "routing": "routing.precedence is the order in which the intents of one turn win the reply (docs/SPEC.md, global intents), with delete_data ahead of stop so that 'erase my info and hang up' deletes first. 'redaction' stands for a redacted or masked number. The first entry present gives the reply key in routing.reply. close_phase: while the pending question is close.anything_else, a stop intent or a done phrase ('no, that's all', 'no, thanks', 'eso es todo') ends the call with close.goodbye, not stop.goodbye; 'that's all' is never a stop keyword."
  },
